{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency","id":1341251,"title":"On Jade Currency","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-14T07:23:38-07:00","id":1341251,"title":"On Jade Currency","content":"&quot;A jade talent is a thin slab of jade weighing 68 pounds.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Jade Talent is roughly scored to form eight rectangular bricks, with the Imperial Treasury\u2019s seal lightly scored on each of the resulting panel facets. The minting date and identifying number are also carved into one or each side of the slab. Some Talents, particularly illegal ones, are unmarked as while the penalty of owning unmarked Jade is confiscation and a hefty fine, the penalty for forging the Treasury\u2019s marks is death.<br /> <br /> By its weight a Jade Talent is worth 12 Bars or 1,536 Obols, but on paper it is worth 8 Bars or 1,024 Obols as a third of its weight is &quot;lost&quot; into Jade powder. The resultant powder is used to craft Jade-steel arms and armour. Physical Talents do not tend to circulate due to difficulty in transportation and enormous value. They either sit in a vault and are traded on paper, are used for building manses, or cut into smaller denominations.<br /> <br /> Jade Bar is a brick-shaped block of Jade with the seal of the Imperial Treasury lightly scored on each face, and is further scored to represent eight smaller strips of slabs of Mina. It is labelled with a carving date and a serial number to discourage fraud. It weighs about eight and a half pounds, and is worth about eight and a half Minae depending on exact weight. On paper it is worth exactly eight Minae. Like the Talent, it is rarely used as physical currency.<br /> <br /> Mina weighs slightly more than a pound, and is a slab of Jade about three inches wide, six inches long, and a quarter-inch thick. It is scored in half-squares, and each half is further scored into eight closely spaced circles, into a total of 16 circles. On the other side of the circles are scored the seals of the Imperial Treasury. By weight, a Mina is worth about three Shekels, on paper it is exactly two Shekels.<br /> <br /> Shekel is a thin square slab of Jade graven with eight circles with the seal of the Imperial Treasury scored inside them on its square side and milled around its thin edges to discourage Jade shaving. A Shekel weighs about nine or ten ounces, and on paper is worth eight Obols.<br /> <br /> Obol <i>always</i> weighs an ounce, and is used as a balance weighs by herb-merchants and drug dealers to demonstrate accurate measurements. The coin is about an inch in diameter, and about 3/8th of an inch in thickness. One side is graven with the seal of the Imperial Treasury, while the other bears an image used during the time of the carving.<br /> <br /> Bit is an illegal modification of the Obol, created by cutting it into four pieces. While it is illegal, the law is not enforced due to its usefulness. Peasants, believing in Jade having innate magical properties, often drill a hole in a Bit and carve symbols on them and wear the result as a charm. Surprisingly they represent roughly 40% of the physically active Jade coinage in the Realm.<br /> <br /> It is illegal for peasants to possess even a single Bit of Jade.<br /> <br /> Exalted 1st Edition: Manacle and Coin has images of the Jade currency: <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/8ifVJr.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Talent, Bar, Mina</a>, and <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/Tyg0TU.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Shekel, Obol, and Bit</a>.<br /> <br /> Exalted 2nd Edition: Corebook also has images of the Jade currency: <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/7SLg9c.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">all six of them</a>.<br /> <br /> Exalted 3rd Edition: Corebook also has images of Jade currency, but they are... Erroneous, to say the least: <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/t8AXLy.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Talent&quot;</a>, <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/QnM4la.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Minae&quot;</a> I presume, and <a href=\"https://horobox.co.uk/u/u6iwmN.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Shekel&quot; and some Obols</a><br /> <br /> Calculating from a Mina\u2019s size, a Talent is roughly 48x24 inches/4x2 feet or roughly 122x61 centimetres (3 inches x 8 (Mina-&gt;Bar) = 24 x 2 (Bar-&gt;Talent) = 48, 6 x 4 (Mina/Bar-&gt; Talent) = 24) in width and length, and I\u2019d say somewhat thicker than Mina\u2019s 1/4th inches thickness due to the scorings it has gone through. Maybe \u00bd inch to an inch in thickness.<br /> <br /> Sources:<br /> Exalted 1st Edition Manacle and Coin pages 104-105<br /> Exalted 2nd Edition Core Rulebook pages 356-358<br /> Exalted 3rd Edition Core Rulebook page 79","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T19:07:28-07:00","id":1341376,"title":"","content":"2nd edition also states that White Jade is the only jade used for currency, as its optimal for the stabilizing effects of the Order Conferring Trade Pattern. They seem to ignore this though in 3rd ed, at least as far as pictures depicting currency is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T16:31:22-07:00","id":1341518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341376#post1341376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd edition also states that White Jade is the only jade used for currency, as its optimal for the stabilizing effects of the Order Conferring Trade Pattern. They seem to ignore this though in 3rd ed, at least as far as pictures depicting currency is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could I ask for a book/page source?<br /> I've tried looking for something to that effect in various books but haven't found a specification for <i>White</i> Jade, just Jade.<br /> <br /> It does make sense that most of the Jade Currency the Realm uses would be White Jade though, since, well, <i>Pole of Earth</i>, but it wouldn't make much sense to just not use the other colours, at least in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T23:35:38-07:00","id":1341579,"title":"","content":"I dont know the source, but I do know that the Order Conferring Trade Pattern was a First Age thing and didnt see use again until the Guild adopted parts of it in its founding. So, The Realm may not use just White Jade anymore, and the Guild standard is silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T00:15:50-07:00","id":1341582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>imadaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341518#post1341518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could I ask for a book/page source?<br /> I've tried looking for something to that effect in various books but haven't found a specification for <i>White</i> Jade, just Jade.<br /> <br /> It does make sense that most of the Jade Currency the Realm uses would be White Jade though, since, well, <i>Pole of Earth</i>, but it wouldn't make much sense to just not use the other colours, at least in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odenels Codex page 20: The Realm uses white jade for its official currency because it resists wear and is so readily available.<br /> <br /> Masters of Jade page 42: The Guild\u2019s silver coinage is less potent in strengthening Creation than jade currency would be","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T01:17:10-07:00","id":1341593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341582#post1341582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odenels Codex page 20: The Realm uses white jade for its official currency because it resists wear and is so readily available.<br /> <br /> Masters of Jade page 42: The Guild\u2019s silver coinage is less potent in strengthening Creation than jade currency would be</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for taking point, good looking out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T02:37:59-07:00","id":1341604,"title":"","content":"If they're supposed to make artifacts out of the jade dust that comes off when they carve the talents into smaller bits then logically they would use all 5 types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T03:31:34-07:00","id":1341608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341604#post1341604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're supposed to make artifacts out of the jade dust that comes off when they carve the talents into smaller bits then logically they would use all 5 types.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they use the dust to make jade-steel alloy (not a real alloy) which is used for artifacts. There's nothing to suggest this is the only source of jade for artifacts (though Odenels Codex does suggest just going to the bank and walking out with large slabs of money to carve into artifacts). And really you want your armor made of white jade.<br /> <br /> Jade of all colors is probably used as money. It's just that white jade is ideal for Realm money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T05:41:03-07:00","id":1341618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341579#post1341579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Order Conferring Trade Pattern was a First Age thing and didnt see use again until the Guild adopted parts of it in its founding. </div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't really; a bunch of cultists who misunderstood it as something you could profit from praying to were just easy enough marks to provide the starting capital.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341604#post1341604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're supposed to make artifacts out of the jade dust that comes off when they carve the talents into smaller bits then logically they would use all 5 types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think imperial boot polish is supposed to be read as meaning that when they grind down the jade coins, they don't let any go to waste it's too valuable for that. There's no reason that a non-denominational block of jade can't be ground to dust, regardless of its colour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341608#post1341608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And really you want your armor made of white jade</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jade of all colors is probably used as money. It's just that white jade is ideal for Realm money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, so few people are allowed to use jade as money, and so little of it will actually be physically changing hands, coming in multiple colours probably didn't make much difference.<br /> <br /> I think viewing it largely in terms of being white from coming from the Blessed Isle forgets that a lot of the Realm's jade is provided in tribute from the Threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T06:09:50-07:00","id":1341620,"title":"","content":"They might have a mint for each jade colour. One in the middle that uses white jade, one near the west coast that uses black jade, one near the east that uses green jade, one in the southern parts that uses red jade and one in the north that uses blue jade. <br /> <br /> Helps trace where a coin came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T06:55:27-07:00","id":1341621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341618#post1341618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't really; a bunch of cultists who misunderstood it as something you could profit from praying to were just easy enough marks to provide the starting capital.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My point had more to do with it being a First Age thing, and thus not really relevant as to whether or not White Jade is currently used as currency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T07:01:40-07:00","id":1341623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341620#post1341620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might have a mint for each jade colour. One in the middle that uses white jade, one near the west coast that uses black jade, one near the east that uses green jade, one in the southern parts that uses red jade and one in the north that uses blue jade. <br /> <br /> Helps trace where a coin came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think M&amp;C and Compass Blessed Isle stated all the coinage in minted in a central manse... I want to say in Juche Province (possibly in Jade River). I'll check later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:10:24-07:00","id":1341658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341620#post1341620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might have a mint for each jade colour. One in the middle that uses white jade, one near the west coast that uses black jade, one near the east that uses green jade, one in the southern parts that uses red jade and one in the north that uses blue jade. <br /> <br /> Helps trace where a coin came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a large logistical burden with little to no payoff. For one thing, origin can also be traced with a stamp.<br /> <br /> For another, I'm not sure it's a pressing concern when minting currency is an imperial monopoly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341621#post1341621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point had more to do with it being a First Age thing, and thus not really relevant as to whether or not White Jade is currently used as currency.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. <br /> <br /> You know, I'm wondering where the idea of jade being used like that first came up. Manacle &amp; Coin describes finance as a means of bulwarking reality, but it seems to be taking place at a scope far beyond reliance on physical currency transportation. There's a reference to deals worth billions of jade talents, but I'm suddenly wondering if that's using the economy of the Realm as a reference point rather than their own standard.<br /> <br /> After all... no, wait, earlier the book says that a jade standard has precedent in the Old Realm, although perhaps not over the whole length of its history. Nevermind anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341251-on-jade-currency?p=1341623#post1341623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think M&amp;C and Compass Blessed Isle stated all the coinage in minted in a central manse... I want to say in Juche Province (possibly in Jade River). I'll check later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Juche was previously a major mining and manufacturing center, so it was a logical spot for the mint. The current location of the Imperial Mint is within the palace itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}